  "text": "One line saws sideways in a sudden jerk, and a forest floor of dead words that feed the living ones. A planet whose languages have no nouns, only verbs and adjectives. An easel stands before a window, its canvas showing the exact slice of meadow and sky that the window itself frames, painted so precisely the two merge into one surface. In a kitchen a white goose, a house, a house, a woman with hair to the floor and a cluster of marbles sits at its center like tiny planets caught in orbit. A boy lives on an asteroid so small he can watch the sunset forty-four times a day by moving his chair.",
